he Thorn Witch shrank with every star, smaller, smaller, till only a grumble remained. The Grumble King, indeed."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'Starlight Restored', 'text': "the Briar Vale celebrated: the fireflies spelled Sage's name, the oak dropped acorns of thanks, the wise owl composed a ballad with a loyal dog as the hero — a loyal dog insisted Sage was the hero; they compromised on both.\n\na singing shell chose to stay with Sage — or Sage chose to stay with it; by now they weren't sure there was a difference. It sits by the bed, glowing softly, a nightlight of pure story.\n\nThey carried the starlight home to the Briar Vale in a singing shell, which had grown to hold it all. The brook ran forward again. The mushrooms glowed gold. The stars came back, one by one, like friends returning."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Promise Kept', 'text': "a loyal dog is older now, greyer, no less brave. They still walk together, still argue about the ballad, still keep the grumble-jar dusted. Friendship, like starlight, doesn't fade if you tend it.\n\nthe Briar Vale thrives: the enchanted forest enchants, the glade whispers kindly, the meadow moonlights. All because one child picked up a singing shell and one friend said 'together.'\n\nNew children come to hear the story, and Sage tells it true: the fear, the laughter, the moment it almost went wrong. 'Were you scared?' they ask. 'Terrified,' Sage says. 'That's what brave is.'"}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Bedtime', 'text': "And now it's bedtime in the Briar Vale, and a singing shell glows soft, and a loyal dog is telling the story one more time, to one more sleepy listener. 'The end,' a loyal dog says.\n\nkindness is magic. Goodnight.\n\nSleep tight, the Briar Vale. The dark is just the blanket. The light is a singing shell, and a singing shell is here, and Sage is here, and a loyal dog is here."}]}

